      "message": "refactor: use mise bin-paths for dynamic PATH without hardcoded versions\n\n- Replace runtime entrypoint wrapper with build-time path capture\n- Use 'mise bin-paths' to dynamically discover tool directories at build time\n- Write paths to /etc/profile.d/mise-paths.sh for shell sourcing\n- Remove ENTRYPOINT wrapper that was causing hang issues\n- Simplify ENV configuration and consolidate MISE_* variables\n- Source mise-paths.sh in bashrc for interactive shells\n- Maintain version-agnostic approach: no hardcoded ruby/node/python versions\n- Restore libelf-dev dependency needed for C++ ELF reader code\n\nThis approach provides the best of both worlds:\n- Dynamic tool path discovery (no version hardcoding)\n- Reliable execution without runtime overhead\n- Compatible with both Docker and Singularity\n- Auto-sources in login shells via profile script",
